# Adversarial case, ratified by the author 2026-08-04.
# Guards the most plausible C-family import: braces as a block delimiter.
# Braces exist only as map literals, so `{` here starts a map and fails loudly
# rather than opening a block.
#
# Moved 2026-09-29 (defect 131's class, given to defect 133's lane): the
# brace habit is one mistake, so the `{` is its one report and the `}` that
# closes it is its debris, which cost `expected_declaration` again until
# that day. The statements inside are read as the body they are, their own
# mistakes too (`parse/braces.hero`).
function main() {  #~ missing_body
    print(1)
}
